# Deploy-time env baked into the PRODUCTION reasoning engine
# (9136379226620952576) by .github/workflows/deploy.yml via `adk deploy
# --env_file`. This is the engine the Chat bot and the Gemini Enterprise
# registration point at — there is no separate "dev" engine on this path.
#
# The file used to be called deploy-dev.env: it was written (2026-07-17) for an
# engine that was still a test rig, and that engine quietly became production
# when the Chat bot shipped. The name outlived the fact and invited edits meant
# for a dev engine. Renamed so the next editor cannot make that mistake.
#
# Everything not set here comes from config.py defaults; the model location is
# pinned in code because it is a property of the model, not the environment.
# Keep this minimal and secret-free — it ships into the engine.
#
# EMIT_THINKING: the file carried =1 for its whole life and NEVER reached the
# engine (relative --env_file, silently dropped — see deploy.yml), so production
# has always run on the default: off. Pinned to 0 here so that fixing the path
# changes nothing observable. Flipping it to 1 now actually lands: the Chat bot
# filters thought parts (src/agent/client.ts:336) so users would see nothing new,
# but the summaries would reach every other consumer of the engine, Gemini
# Enterprise included, and grow every event payload. That is a decision to take
# deliberately, not a side effect of a path fix.
EMIT_THINKING=0

# The sandbox is a property of the deploy, not of callers: this flag is what
# makes production ignore a `state.sandbox` override entirely. Explicit, because
# a missing key would also read as off and would not record the intent.
# CI pins this (tests/unit/test_deploy_env_isolation.py).
SANDBOX_ENABLED=0
